1
00:00:03,334 --> 00:00:06,373
OK, Philip. This is your third cup of coffee.

2
00:00:06,373 --> 00:00:08,459
We should get to work,

3
00:00:08,459 --> 00:00:10,434
or we won't be finished by dinnertime.

4
00:00:10,434 --> 00:00:12,912
I guess we must.

5
00:00:12,912 --> 00:00:13,912
We must.

6
00:00:13,912 --> 00:00:27,462
OK. The beginning of my famous Thanksgiving apple pie.

7
00:00:27,462 --> 00:00:34,651
One apple. Two apples. Three apples. Four apples.

8
00:00:34,651 --> 00:00:37,107
Come on, Philip!

9
00:00:37,107 --> 00:00:39,214
Get busy with your famous apple pie.

10
00:00:39,214 --> 00:00:41,692
There's much more to be done.

11
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:47,647
Now, the ingredients.

12
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:50,625
What goes into my apple pie besides apples?

13
00:00:50,625 --> 00:01:05,515
Ah, yes. Flour, sugar, butter.

14
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:12,413
Butter, nice and cold and hard.

15
00:01:12,413 --> 00:01:13,679
OK, here are the walnuts.

16
00:01:13,679 --> 00:01:15,306
Last but not least,

17
00:01:15,306 --> 00:01:24,883
the reason my apple pie is famous--cinnamon.

18
00:01:24,883 --> 00:01:25,383
Cinnamon ...

19
00:01:25,383 --> 00:01:26,050
Ellen, where's the cinnamon?

20
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:26,914
If there is any cinnamon,

21
00:01:26,914 --> 00:01:36,064
it's in the cabinet with the salt and pepper.

22
00:01:36,064 --> 00:01:39,141
Salt, pepper, dill weed, garlic powder, cinnamon. Ellen?

23
00:01:39,141 --> 00:01:39,910
Yes, Philip.

24
00:01:39,910 --> 00:01:44,229
Is it possible that we forgot to buy cinnamon?

25
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:52,457
Yes, it is possible that we forgot to buy cinnamon.

26
00:01:52,457 --> 00:01:57,560
Well, how can I make my famous apple pie without cinnamon?

27
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:58,128
Good morning.

28
00:01:58,128 --> 00:02:02,776
Oh, hi, Robbie. Good morning.

29
00:02:02,776 --> 00:02:03,736
Good morning. Robbie.

30
00:02:03,736 --> 00:02:06,327
Can you do me a favor?

31
00:02:06,327 --> 00:02:07,267
Sure, Dad. What?

32
00:02:07,267 --> 00:02:10,052
Remember my apple pie on Thanksgiving?

33
00:02:10,052 --> 00:02:13,030
What do you love about it?

34
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:14,008
The apples?

35
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:19,964
No. The sssss...

36
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:20,964
Cinnamon.

37
00:02:20,964 --> 00:02:24,942
Right. We don't have any cinnamon.

38
00:02:24,942 --> 00:02:27,647
I'll go down to Henry's grocery. He's always open.

39
00:02:27,647 --> 00:02:28,898
I'll get some for you.

40
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:31,876
That's my boy!

41
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:33,756
Oh, put your heavy jacket on, Robbie.

42
00:02:33,756 --> 00:02:37,832
It's cold outside.

43
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:40,810
Alexandra might call.

44
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:42,810
Tell her I'll call her right back.

45
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:43,788
OK.

46
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:49,744
Thanks, Son.

47
00:02:49,744 --> 00:03:05,607
Uh, why does he always have to slam the door?

48
00:03:05,607 --> 00:03:10,589
Hello.... Hello, Alexandra. How are you? ... Fine.

49
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:12,589
Robbie just went to the store.

50
00:03:12,589 --> 00:03:13,567
He'll be back soon.

51
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:15,407
He said he'll call you.

52
00:03:15,407 --> 00:03:21,043
... Oh, oh, I see.... Oh ... certainly. ...

53
00:03:21,043 --> 00:03:22,501
Well, do you have the phone number there?

54
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:28,457
... Oh ... I see.... Please, I know he wants to talk to you.... ...

55
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:29,657
Thank you,

56
00:03:29,657 --> 00:03:34,413
and happy Thanksgiving to you and your family, too.

57
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:40,251
Try to come by later for dessert.... Bye.

58
00:03:40,251 --> 00:03:40,945
That was Alexandra.

59
00:03:40,945 --> 00:03:42,097
She and the Molinas

60
00:03:42,097 --> 00:03:45,347
are going to spend Thanksgiving with their cousins.

61
00:03:45,347 --> 00:03:46,325
She doesn't have the phone number.

62
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:49,303
Oh, Robbie will be disappointed.

63
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:52,281
He'll be grouchy.

64
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:55,259
Maybe she'll call back. She promised.

65
00:03:55,259 --> 00:04:04,193
Here's your cinnamon, Pop.

66
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:10,149
It was a dollar and sixty cents.

67
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:13,127
You forgot to ask me for the change.

68
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:22,060
Or did you forget to give it to me?

69
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:25,038
Thanks, Son.

70
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:28,016
Alexandra called.

71
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:29,340
I'll call her back.

72
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:31,610
She said she'll call you later.

73
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:42,906
She's not at home.

74
00:04:42,906 --> 00:04:45,246
You should have your breakfast, Son.

75
00:04:45,246 --> 00:04:45,884
Make you feel better.

76
00:04:45,884 --> 00:04:49,166
Protein, vitamins.

77
00:04:49,166 --> 00:04:50,782
She said she'll call back?

78
00:04:50,782 --> 00:04:52,773
Yes, she did.

79
00:04:52,773 --> 00:04:55,485
Good morning, everyone!

80
00:04:55,485 --> 00:04:58,796
Happy Turkey Day!

81
00:04:58,796 --> 00:05:00,774
What's wrong?

82
00:05:00,774 --> 00:05:04,752
Nothing. Absolutely nothing.

83
00:05:04,752 --> 00:05:06,419
What's gotten into him?

84
00:05:06,419 --> 00:05:09,230
He missed a phone call.

85
00:05:09,230 --> 00:05:09,708
From ...?

86
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:13,011
Yes, Alexandra.

87
00:05:13,011 --> 00:05:18,642
It's nice to see young love.... Oh, to be young again!

88
00:05:18,642 --> 00:05:21,642
Where's the coffee?
